WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Christians believe that
Jesus' life, death,

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:08.050
resurrection and ascension rescued
the world from sin and death.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.840
Catholics call that whole
story the Paschal Mystery.

4
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.020
If the rescue has already happened,
it sounds as if the job is done.

5
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.050
So if Jesus has already saved the world,
why do Catholics say they are still being

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.440
saved?

7
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:26.730
In this mission, you'll meet a short word
that Catholic teaching leans on again

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.210
and again: grace.

9
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.790
You'll find out what Catholics mean
by sanctifying grace and actual grace,

10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.400
and where they believe grace is found.

11
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: find out why Catholics
speak of still being saved.
